# Opsphere — DevOps Operational Intelligence

Opsphere connects your DevOps tools to **Cursor** and **Codex**. Query logs, check deploys, search issues, diagnose incidents, and manage integrations — all from the chat, without leaving the IDE.

The backend is a remote MCP server. All tool calls go to the Opsphere gateway. No tool logic runs locally.

---

## Available Tool Categories

These tools are available once authenticated and integrations are configured:

| Category | Provider | Tools |
|----------|----------|-------|
| Monitoring | Datadog | `dd_logs_search`, `dd_errors_by_service`, `dd_errors_recent`, `dd_synthetics_summary` |
| Deployments | Multi-stack (catalog) | **`deployment_status`** (preferred) — Vercel, CI, GitOps, S3+CloudFront, ECS from your configured sources |
| Deployments | Vercel (direct) | `vercel_deploys_latest`, `vercel_project_status` — only when user asks Vercel-only or `deployment_status` gaps suggest it |
| Deployments | Railway (direct) | `railway_projects_list`, `railway_project_status`, `railway_deployments_latest`, `railway_logs`, `railway_health_summary`, `railway_incident_diagnosis` — 17 read-only tools when Railway module is enabled |
| Source Control | GitHub Enterprise | `ghe_repo_summary`, `ghe_actions_latest` |
| Source Control | Bitbucket | `bb_pipelines_latest`, `bb_pipeline_diagnose` |
| CDN / DNS | Cloudflare | `cf_quick_status`, `cf_dns_records` |
| Issue Tracking | Jira | `jira_issue_get`, `jira_issues_search` |
| Error Tracking | Sentry | `sentry_issues_list`, `sentry_issues_search` |
| Code Quality | SonarQube (paid) | `sq_projects_search` (URL or key) → `sq_last_scan_summary` for last scan; `sq_quality_gate_status` + `sq_issues_search` for QG drill-down — prompt `diagnose-sonarqube-quality-gate` when in playbooks |
| Search | Algolia (paid) | `alg_indices_list`, `alg_index_settings`, `alg_search`, `alg_object_get`, `alg_logs` — configure with App ID + restricted API key |
| Cloud | AWS | `aws_sts_whoami`, `aws_cli_query`, `aws_bedrock_agent_diagnose`, `aws_lambda_agent_diagnose` (Bedrock Agents — paid `aws` module) |
| Network (built-in) | — | `dns_lookup`, `http_check`, `cert_status`, `alg_status`, `alg_incidents` |
| Integration Mgmt | — | `ops_configure_integration`, `ops_list_integrations`, `ops_test_integration`, `ops_remove_integration` |
| Plan & Usage | — | `ops_my_usage` |
| Work context | — | `ops_set_work_context`, `ops_get_work_context` |
| **Connection Hub** (broker) | — | `ops_accounts_list`, `ops_account_link_start`, `ops_account_unlink`, `ops_context_open`, `ops_context_close` — only when `tools/list` includes them |
| Operational memory | — | `memory_search`, `memory_store`, `memory_session_touch`, `memory_invalidate` |
| **Macro workflows** (Team+) | — | `macro_outage_triage`, `macro_endpoint_health`, `macro_env_health` — composite read-only runs with SSE progress |

**Network tools (`dns_lookup`, `http_check`, `cert_status`, `alg_status`, `alg_incidents`) work immediately after login — no integration setup needed.** `alg_status` / `alg_incidents` report **global** Algolia platform health (not your tenant App ID).

**Macro tools** (`macro_*`) appear only on **Team / Enterprise** when the `macros` module is enabled. They run multi-step investigations server-side with progress streaming. Use skill **`run-macro-workflows`** when `tools/list` includes them; otherwise use subagents (`/outage-triage`, `/endpoint-health`) or atomic network tools.

**Memory tools** appear only when the `memory` module is enabled for your tenant (`tenant_tools`, profile `cursor`). They store **distilled** notes from past sessions — not live ops truth. Always verify current state with Datadog, K8s, Vercel, or other live tools after reading memory.

**Work context** is injected automatically when MCP connects (default cloud account + index of others). After signup, if `ops_my_usage` shows work context as not configured, run the `set-work-context` skill. For full text of a non-default account, use `ops_get_work_context` or resource `opsphere://tenant/account-context`.

**Connection Hub** (when `ops_accounts_list` is in `tools/list`): new signups may get a Hub anchor tenant — not an operational workspace. Link client workspaces with skill **`link-account`**, then **`open-work-context`** before any tenant-scoped tool. Pass `context_id` on every scoped call; use `ops_context_close` before switching. Hub rejects `ops_configure_integration` / `ops_set_work_context` without an open context on a linked tenant.

### MCP resources (gateway — read via @ or Fetch MCP Resource)

Eleven read-only resources ship with the remote MCP server (nine universal + two Hub-only). They are **not** duplicated in this plugin repo — Cursor/Codex fetch them from the gateway after Connect.

| URI | When to read |
|-----|----------------|
| `opsphere://rules/operational` | Full tool catalog + tenant scope (same as server instructions; refreshes with catalog) |
| `opsphere://tools/catalog` | JSON: enabled modules + prompt index for your tenant |
| `opsphere://playbooks/index` | All MCP prompts grouped by category (outage, pipeline, SonarQube, Bedrock `investigate-bedrock-agent`, …) |
| `opsphere://tenant/account-context` | Full per-account `system_prompt_context` (infra names, regions, capabilities) |
| `opsphere://hub/active-context` | **Hub only** — active `context_id`, connection label, expiry |
| `opsphere://hub/connections` | **Hub only** — linked connections list (same data as `ops_accounts_list`) |
| `opsphere://policies/change-approval` | Before mutating Cloudflare / Akamai / `system_update` |
| `opsphere://policies/secrets-handling` | Credential handling and redaction |
| `opsphere://policies/incident-response` | Incident lifecycle and roles |
| `opsphere://taxonomy/severity` | SEV1–4 definitions and confidence |
| `opsphere://inventory/critical-assets` | Canonical brands, accounts, regions, apps |

**When to use resources vs tools:** use **`deployment_status`**, **`macro_*`**, or atomic tools for live checks. Use **`opsphere://tenant/account-context`** when you need full catalog prose for a non-default account. Use **`opsphere://playbooks/index`** to discover guided prompts (e.g. `diagnose-sonarqube-quality-gate`, `investigate-bedrock-agent`). Do not expect one resource per tool — the catalog lives in `opsphere://rules/operational`.

