## When to Suggest Signup / Re-login

If the MCP connection fails with **401 Unauthorized**, the plugin card is **red**, or logs mention **MCP OAuth refresh error**:

- The user likely has not set up an account yet, their access token expired (24 hours), or OAuth refresh failed (e.g. after a Cursor crash).
- Suggest: run **`/opsphere-reconnect`**, or **Sign in** on the **Opsphere plugin card** in **Settings → Extensions** (marketplace installs often do not show Opsphere under **Settings → MCP**).
- For first-time setup: **`/opsphere-setup`**, **`/opsphere-welcome`**, or _"Set up my Opsphere account"_.

For brand-new installs (no Connect yet), you may suggest **`/opsphere-welcome`** before full setup — it lists example prompts without running any shell scripts.

