## Trial Expiration (TRIAL_EXPIRED)

If the gateway returns error code `TRIAL_EXPIRED`:

- Tell the user: "Your 30-day free trial has expired. Visit **https://opsphere.io/pricing** to continue using Opsphere."
- Do not retry the request.
- Do not suggest re-login — re-authentication will not fix an expired trial.

---

## Rate Limit (RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED)

If the gateway returns error code `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`:

- Tell the user how many calls they have used and when the limit resets (from `details.resetsAt` in the error body).
- Suggest: "You can check your full plan status with `ops_my_usage`."
- Do not retry the request automatically.

---

## Execution policy (informative only — gateway enforces)

The gateway applies **execution policies** on every `tools/call` for your tenant and runtime (`cursor` for this plugin). Limits come from PostgreSQL — **never** send policy fields in tool arguments.

**Never include in `tools/call` arguments:** `tenant_id`, `plan`, `profile_id`, `max_tool_calls`, `max_cost_units`, `max_duration_ms`, `max_retries`, `max_macro_calls`, `allow_sensitive_actions`, `enabled_tools`, `policy_version`, `subscription_id`, `runtime_profile`.

Use `ops_my_usage` for plan/usage visibility. The gateway is the only authority for allow/deny.

### JSON-RPC execution denials

| Code | `data.reason` (examples) | Agent action |
|------|--------------------------|--------------|
| `-32003` | `execution_policy_missing` | Tell user policy is not configured; contact admin — do not retry blindly |
| `-32003` | `execution_module_not_enabled` | Tool/module not on plan — suggest `ops_my_usage` or upgrade |
| `-32003` | `execution_sensitive_action_denied` | Pick a read-only alternative or ask admin to allow sensitive actions |
| `-32003` | `BROKER_CONTEXT_*` | Open Hub context (`open-work-context`) and pass `context_id` |
| `-32004` | `max_tool_calls`, `max_cost_units`, `max_macro_calls` | Budget exhausted — wait for `resetsAt` or reduce scope; do not spam retries |

