## Admin portal vs plugin

| Concern | Community | Team / Enterprise (and Professional) |
|---------|-----------|--------------------------------------|
| **Integrations** (Datadog, AWS keys, GitHub token, …) | Configure in chat with `ops_configure_integration` | Prefer admin portal Cloud Catalog / credentials; plugin still works when `catalog_config_surface` allows |
| **MCP tool modules** (enable K8s, ArgoCD, macros, …) | Fixed by plan matrix — admin **Tools** toggles for out-of-plan modules are disabled | Org admins manage modules in **https://admin.opsphere.io** → Tools |
| **`ops_my_usage`** | Shows plan, usage, enabled tool count; `catalog_config_surface: plugin` | May show `catalog_config_surface: admin_portal` — point users to the admin portal for catalog/module changes |

If a **Community** user asks to enable Kubernetes, ArgoCD, macros, or other premium modules in the admin Tools page: explain those modules are **not included** in Community. Suggest [opsphere.io/pricing](https://opsphere.io/pricing). Do not invent workarounds that toggle premium modules.

If the gateway returns `PLAN_TOOL_NOT_INCLUDED`: the tool is outside the subscription allow-list — same upgrade guidance.

